{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up","id":146704,"title":"Acquiring the Avatar Birthright after God level-up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-23T07:28:42-07:00","id":146704,"title":"Acquiring the Avatar Birthright after God level-up","content":"Can anyone think of an in-game way to acquire an Avatar Birthright after the God level-up if a player did not take it, but later wishes to? Sanctums seem easy enough to explain, but I find myself lacking a sufficient metaphysical process to obtain or improve an Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2692-captain-morganism","name":"Captain Morganism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2692_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:51:19-07:00","id":147179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Morganism</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up#post146704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone think of an in-game way to acquire an Avatar Birthright after the God level-up if a player did not take it, but later wishes to? Sanctums seem easy enough to explain, but I find myself lacking a sufficient metaphysical process to obtain or improve an Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way is to give every god the ability to use Avatar for free, and refund the player the difference in bonus points.<br /> You can then have a more knowledgeable god teach them the process in exchange for a favor (as gods often do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:47:01-07:00","id":147570,"title":"","content":"The Avatar Birthright is stupid. Avatar 5 should just be a free, innate part of Godhood. <br /> <br /> However, if you <i>want</i> to use Avatar as a Birthright and want ideas for justifying its increase, that isn't hard. Treat it like any other trait. You increase it by practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T09:17:27-07:00","id":147863,"title":"","content":"Or just not have it as a Background. By which I mean not have it at all... If you come to town ALL of you comes to town. Not bits and pieces. If you want to act like you're lower powered, just act like it. Almost every mythology has gods wandering around in mufti for one reason or another and no implication that they had reduced or divided themselves to do so. If you want Avatars, make it a part of the PSP for religions that actually HAVE Avatars or an analogous concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:58:05-07:00","id":147973,"title":"","content":"In Scion 2.0, we went the way Telgar mentioned and the ability to 'dim' your godly greatness to whatever you wish is now just a simple side-effect of becoming a god. There are myths that suggest Avatar is an actual power, for example Zeus is not walking around at Epic Appearance 9+ with his mortal lovers. <br /> <br /> But if you're running Scion RAW still and a PC decides that he wants the Avatar birthright later than apotheosis, or increasing it, there's a thousand and one IC reasons that can be attached to it and justified. You can describe it as the player's ichor was still overwhelmed by the rise to divinity and only now is settling down to the point where they can even begin to quench it to &quot;lower&quot; their legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T13:04:44-07:00","id":148077,"title":"","content":"Why is &quot;dimming down his Epic Appearance&quot; a use of Avatar? I thought there was a Knack for that. In fact, a Knack or several seems like a more judicious way to handle it without shoehorning something that doesn't even vaguely fit.<br /> <br /> But then we have a game with Vedic &quot;Titans&quot; so I guess I'll just shut up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T13:42:43-07:00","id":148091,"title":"","content":"You'd also need something to dim down charisma. And to explain how the greeks got involved with the trojan war without violating valor. And reduce the dangers of fateful aura or risk your players being totally incapable of going down to the world without summoning catastrophic shit every time they do. If you don't reduce fateful aura, then mortals need to be taken out of the world to sex up for more scions instead of the other way around. Lots of little things have to be tweaked if you get rid of Avatar.<br /> <br /> But just giving people Avatar as a default part of the god package? That's an easy solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:13:13-07:00","id":148112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148091#post148091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd also need something to dim down charisma. And to explain how the greeks got involved with the trojan war without violating valor. And reduce the dangers of fateful aura or risk your players being totally incapable of going down to the world without summoning catastrophic shit every time they do. If you don't reduce fateful aura, then mortals need to be taken out of the world to sex up for more scions instead of the other way around. Lots of little things have to be tweaked if you get rid of Avatar.<br /> <br /> But just giving people Avatar as a default part of the god package? That's an easy solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what Twitch said, and added to the fact that My Eyes Are Up Here RAW turns off your Epic Appearance for mortals, period. There's no &quot;fine-tuning&quot; it, there's no middle ground, Mortals are frankly unable to perceive your Epic Appearance, and your Mundane Appearance; hell, they won't even recognize you unless you pop MEAUH again.<br /> <br /> So it's not a knack, it's Zeus turning down parts of his godly self to interact with the mortal woman on roughly her level. Hence, Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T20:47:44-07:00","id":148362,"title":"","content":"Zeus doesn't turn down his LEGEND. He turns down his APPEARANCE. So as to not burn and blind and reduce his lovers to ash. (Which Epic Appearance never does anyways...) That's a Knack, even if it's one that needs writing up (and which one of us hasn't ever written up a Knack?) <br /> <br /> In fact, it's probably better to just get rid of My Eyes Are Up Here and have everyone have a dial that controls how much of their Attribute and Epics are in play at any time. Not doing so is like a kick start down a slippery slope. So Zeus needs to use Avatar so he can avoid smashing everything in sight &quot;bull in china shop&quot;-like with his Epic Strength? He's constantly going insane from too much input from his Epic Perception? He can't help making everyone do everything he says because his Epic Manipulation is always on. Everyone falls kneeling in awe and terror from his Epic Charisma. <br /> <br /> Avatars are gods manifesting themselves discretely. Vishnu IS Krisha. He IS Parashurama. They ARE Vishnu. But they are also themselves. That's Avatar. <br /> <br /> The Background reflects neither.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T21:28:00-07:00","id":148370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148362#post148362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Avatars are gods manifesting themselves discretely. Vishnu IS Krisha. He IS Parashurama. They ARE Vishnu. But they are also themselves. That's Avatar.<br /> <br /> The Background reflects neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Avatara and very much a Deva power, and works for them but it shouldn't be a power that every god from every culture has because they did not use the same idea of what a God's avatar was. This is a subject I'm pretty sure Samudra could explain far better than me as we've used his expertise to rewrite the Deva PSP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148362#post148362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, it's probably better to just get rid of My Eyes Are Up Here and have everyone have a dial that controls how much of their Attribute and Epics are in play at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did something else with MEAUH to make it not-suck, but what you just described is very similar to how we run the Avatar birthrigh; except we do not allow selectivity. You can &quot;dial&quot; your Attributes wherever on the scale you want them to be, but it's an all or nothing deal. If you want to walk around as effectively Legend 4 on the world, you can do so. If you want to visit someone and not come down as a full-blown god, that should be part and parcel of the divine package.<br /> <br /> For us, the Avatar birthright is not you making a lower legend copy of yourself; it is you forcibly quenching your legend to appear for all intents and purposes as a lower-legend being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 05-25-2014, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T21:46:11-07:00","id":148375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148362#post148362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it's probably better to just get rid of My Eyes Are Up Here and have everyone have a dial that controls how much of their Attribute and Epics are in play at any time. Not doing so is like a kick start down a slippery slope. So Zeus needs to use Avatar so he can avoid smashing everything in sight &quot;bull in china shop&quot;-like with his Epic Strength? He's constantly going insane from too much input from his Epic Perception? He can't help making everyone do everything he says because his Epic Manipulation is always on. Everyone falls kneeling in awe and terror from his Epic Charisma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if everyone is capable of controlling their Epic Appearance personally, able to flip it off and flip it on, dial it up and dial it down, how do you explain the multitude of myths where being attractive leads to something horrible happening? Where I am sure the person would have dismissed their Epic Appearance in an instant? There is the rape of Demeter, Selene and Endymion, Eos and the multitude of people she molests, Zeus and Ganymede, Medusa and Poseidon, Hermes and Aglaurus, and quite a few more. It's a common theme, especially, as you can see, for the Greeks.<br /> <br /> But, in the scene with Zeus and Semele, it is very specifically mentioned that Zeus is hiding his true divine form from her, as to prevent the obliteration (as is mechanically represented through Gotham By Night's Divine Splendor) that would result if she saw his true form. This isn't that Zeus is toning down his true appearance, but he is concealing his true form from her.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the issues of being overwhelmed by your Epic Perception are already addressed through Parallel Attention, which helps a Scion manage the utterly overwhelming barrage of sensory input that they receive.<br /> <br /> While the issue of having a world made of tissue paper is not addressed for Epic Strength RAW, I have seen Storytellers handle it two ways. One of which is requiring a Knack to prevent harming others, or risk accidentally, for example, maiming a Significant Other in bed. While, I have seen others rule that since we are capable of controlling our strength, Gods can control the extent to which they wield their Epic Strength. Which is quite unlike Epic Appearance, for while someone can control the amount of force they put into objects, they can't control how beautiful they are.<br /> <br /> And yes, those are pretty much perfect examples of how having incredibly high Epic Manipulation and Charisma works at high Legends when facing beings with low resistances, such as mortals. If Baldur walked down the streets of Reykjavik as a Legend 12 God, all the mortals who saw him would love him for eternity, the love they could share with each other being as pale as a piece of gravel compared to the majesty of the Sun itself. <br /> <br /> But! Ultimately, this is up to the individual Storyteller. While I am not one myself, Iry, Aynie, Telgar, John, and Anne all use some different pieces of this as an ever present reality for the Scions, and the Gods. Though, every single storyteller can obviously run the game in whatever way they wish, not a single one of us uses RAW Scion in its entirety, everyone is entirely welcome to interpret the rules and the universe as they wish, and no one is any more correct than anyone else for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:41:56-07:00","id":148743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148375#post148375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But, in the scene with Zeus and Semele, it is very specifically mentioned that Zeus is hiding his true divine form from her, as to prevent the obliteration (as is mechanically represented through Gotham By Night's Divine Splendor) that would result if she saw his true form. This isn't that Zeus is toning down his true appearance, but he is concealing his true form from her.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Your example in no way implies a use of Avatar. It is either using My Eyes Are Up Here or Zeus controlling his Appearance. Like I said, there is a difference between controlling the use of EPICS and the use of LEGEND. Having people reduce their Legend is a ham-fisted, overbearing and, frankly, stupid-for-the-god-in-question way of doing it. Why? Want to kill or control Zeus, wait until he goes to see his lady-friend. He just doesn't measure up. He's toast. <br /> <br /> Gods who make people melt are usually examples of gods being careless or possessing hubris. A divine &quot;oops&quot; situation. <br /> <br /> In actual Avatar-as-they-are-handled-in-myth, which all of the people mentioned use as their ultimate reason for handling things one way or the other, a god separates a part of him or herself off as a semi-independant entity that is still them. Vishnu doesn't change into Krishna. Krishna is running around doing his fun stuff and there is still a Vishnu. That's Avatar. (a word that gets heavily abused and over-used in Scion anyways. It is bad design to have the same word mean multiple different things.) Anne does handle this concept pretty well with her Mayan PSP. <br /> <br /> And, having said that, I can also advocate getting rid of it as a difficult, clunky and unwieldy mechanism that doesn't reflect the concept it's trying to embody in pretty much any way, shape or form. I don't agree with the way some of those people (John, Anne, Telgar) use Avatar to explain away things in myth that don't fit their conceptions. Specific example. the Trojan War. Telgar and I have had intense discussion about whether Diomedes could actually really wound Ares and Aphrodite (who, by the way interacted with mortals all the time, with them knowing she was Aphrodite without them just melting at how insanely beautiful she was, or becoming her devoted slaves.) (Note: These occurred BEFORE Zeus banned the gods from interfering.) Anne, John and Telgar say those have to be Avatars to be defeated by mere mortals. I say Diomedes was a kick-ass mortal (with a fair bit of divine ancestry more than 3 generations back) who did catch a couple of petty, willfull, condescending and ignorant gods off guard and do the unthinkable. Anne/John/Telgar all maintain that had to be a use of Avatar because otherwise no mortal can ever do anything to a god ever. I don't agree with them on the relative potential coolness of mortals and/or the concept of divine beings being nigh omnipotent but just fucking up from time to time in this particular way as they do in so many others. <br /> <br /> We don't even have to agree to disagree. Pundits on the subject certainly don't. I think I'm right and they're wrong. They, the opposite. We each get to advocate our positions and we never ever have to come to a compromise. Doesn't stop me from discussing and hashing out things Hittite with Anne. Doesn't stop me from being in Telgar's game, while enjoying it thoroughly and and completely disagreeing with him on the use or existence of the Avatar background. <br /> <br /> By my prefence, I'd handle the concept of a couple of ways. Not making the gods have powers over which they have no control. That seems pretty nice. I like the fact that I, as a player, and the people in my game are going to have to invest in something separate to take care of something that makes them unwieldy and more difficult to play. If not that, then have the gods running amok tearing holes in the world and the fabric of civilization by accident unless they invest in something much less dear than a build point at apotheosis and make it a set of Knacks like My Eyes Are Up Here. Make the concept of Avatar something that is and make it pantheon appropriate, meaning part of the PSP for pantheons that are into that sort of thing (Devas and Mayan gods LEAP to mind). Otherwise make it part of a Purview about interacting with mortals that everyone can buy and letting players decide if they want to purchase relevant Boons from a robust &quot;Boon Cloud&quot;. (I prefer the former).<br /> <br /> Hopefully Scion 2.0 will either eliminate Avatar as is or integrate into the character substrate at apotheosis in a more elegant and appropriate way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T11:17:37-07:00","id":148799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your example in no way implies a use of Avatar. It is either using My Eyes Are Up Here or Zeus controlling his Appearance. Like I said, there is a difference between controlling the use of EPICS and the use of LEGEND. Having people reduce their Legend is a ham-fisted, overbearing and, frankly, stupid-for-the-god-in-question way of doing it. Why? Want to kill or control Zeus, wait until he goes to see his lady-friend. He just doesn't measure up. He's toast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I personally believe that the example of Zeus and Semele is a strong contender towards Avatars, but it's just an opinion really, I'm no more right than you are. But, to explain your point that a God could just be offed when in an Avatar, I know that some Storytellers run it like that in order to make choosing to descend to earth a very big deal for the Gods, for it carries great risks, but, for example, Telgar runs it where if your Avatar dies, you just pop back to your Sanctum, and in Scion 2.0 we run it roughly similar, but with a greater penalty. I believe in RAW it is the same, but I would have to go and check.<br /> <br /> But, asides from the troubles of Epic Attributes, the Legendary Aura is actually one of the two main reasons Avatars are a thing. The Legendary Aura is a very basic, and omnipresent concept in the game, and all of the large scale revisions of it that I have seen. The higher Legend you have, the more dramatic stuff Fate is going to drive your way. Zeus can't hang around Greece at his full power, or Typhon may 'just happen' to break free and try to kill him again.<br /> <br /> Additionally, while RAW fails to accomplish this mechanically, the lower Legend you are, and the less likely you are to gain new Fates when you are at a lower Legend. GBN, Telgar, and Scion 2.0 all use this concept, though to different degrees.<br /> <br /> But, ultimately, we use Avatars because it helps with Epic Attributes, Fateful Aura, and Fates. You are entirely welcome to disagree, but that is the way we run it. We are no more right than you are, just a difference of opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In actual Avatar-as-they-are-handled-in-myth, which all of the people mentioned use as their ultimate reason for handling things one way or the other, a god separates a part of him or herself off as a semi-independant entity that is still them. Vishnu doesn't change into Krishna. Krishna is running around doing his fun stuff and there is still a Vishnu. That's Avatar. (a word that gets heavily abused and over-used in Scion anyways. It is bad design to have the same word mean multiple different things.) Anne does handle this concept pretty well with her Mayan PSP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, Avatar is a word far too often used in Scion. But, the way we handle the differnces between the Avatara of the Deva and the Avatars of the rest of the Divine is that the Avataras are independent beings, able to interact with the world while the God or Goddess is off doing other things. We are currently working on the mechanics of the God Rank Atman Boons, so we have no direct mechanics on paper yet, but the main difference is to be that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, having said that, I can also advocate getting rid of it as a difficult, clunky and unwieldy mechanism that doesn't reflect the concept it's trying to embody in pretty much any way, shape or form. I don't agree with the way some of those people (John, Anne, Telgar) use Avatar to explain away things in myth that don't fit their conceptions. Specific example. the Trojan War. Telgar and I have had intense discussion about whether Diomedes could actually really wound Ares and Aphrodite (who, by the way interacted with mortals all the time, with them knowing she was Aphrodite without them just melting at how insanely beautiful she was, or becoming her devoted slaves.) (Note: These occurred BEFORE Zeus banned the gods from interfering.) Anne, John and Telgar say those have to be Avatars to be defeated by mere mortals. I say Diomedes was a kick-ass mortal (with a fair bit of divine ancestry more than 3 generations back) who did catch a couple of petty, willfull, condescending and ignorant gods off guard and do the unthinkable. Anne/John/Telgar all maintain that had to be a use of Avatar because otherwise no mortal can ever do anything to a god ever. I don't agree with them on the relative potential coolness of mortals and/or the concept of divine beings being nigh omnipotent but just fucking up from time to time in this particular way as they do in so many others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, the scene in the Illiad is prone to much, much debate. Personally, I believe that it is a prime example of Avatars in work, but you are entirely able to disagree. I, personally, believe that when Aphrodite appears to some mortals she is defiantly Avatared down, or invisible, something which the Theoi do quite often. But, for example, when she appears to Anchises, she is not Avatared down and the world just explodes with copulating big cats and how stunning she is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't even have to agree to disagree. Pundits on the subject certainly don't. I think I'm right and they're wrong. They, the opposite. We each get to advocate our positions and we never ever have to come to a compromise. Doesn't stop me from discussing and hashing out things Hittite with Anne. Doesn't stop me from being in Telgar's game, while enjoying it thoroughly and and completely disagreeing with him on the use or existence of the Avatar background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course you don't have to agree to disagree, but personally, I feel like just having an argument about it past this point is needless. If neither of us are going to be able to convince the other, wouldn't it just be better to not waste the time and energy of each other and agree do disagree? I don't believe I am right, or that you are, just that we have different ways in which we would like to handle Avatars in our games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my prefence, I'd handle the concept of a couple of ways. Not making the gods have powers over which they have no control. That seems pretty nice. I like the fact that I, as a player, and the people in my game are going to have to invest in something separate to take care of something that makes them unwieldy and more difficult to play. If not that, then have the gods running amok tearing holes in the world and the fabric of civilization by accident unless they invest in something much less dear than a build point at apotheosis and make it a set of Knacks like My Eyes Are Up Here. Make the concept of Avatar something that is and make it pantheon appropriate, meaning part of the PSP for pantheons that are into that sort of thing (Devas and Mayan gods LEAP to mind). Otherwise make it part of a Purview about interacting with mortals that everyone can buy and letting players decide if they want to purchase relevant Boons from a robust &quot;Boon Cloud&quot;. (I prefer the former).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an entirely appropriate way to handle things, I would really love to see what you come up with. I really do adore looking at other people's house rules, so if you ever devote yours to somewhere online, please let me know. I would love to see your Enech, and your Avatar stuff, but only if it's no bother to you and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148743#post148743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully Scion 2.0 will either eliminate Avatar as is or integrate into the character substrate at apotheosis in a more elegant and appropriate way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Scion 2.0 currently handles it in the way Aynie and myself have been describing, though we are fussing with it at the moment. It will be up on the site when we post it. But, I believe you may mean Scion Second Eddition, and I am too quite rivited to see how they handle different things. I do hope they are able to improve on the pitfalls, such as, as you mentioned, the overabundance of terms using &quot;Avatar&quot; as their name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 05-25-2014, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T13:22:24-07:00","id":148908,"title":"","content":"<b>The single biggest issue is Fateful Aura.</b> Without something like Avatar to reduce your permanent legend, Fateful Aura is going to have catastrophic consequences for anywhere you visit as a god.<br /> <br /> One possible solution is to change Fateful Aura, but it is already one of the most important rules that inform the setting of Scion, a powerful motivator for parties to stay active, and an invaluable aid to Scion Storytellers in general. Another possible solution is to create magic spells that temporarily reduce the impact of Fateful Aura. However, the logistics of this option are rather messy.<br /> <br /> <b>Thoughts?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T09:27:02-07:00","id":149444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=148799#post148799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, of course you don't have to agree to disagree, but personally, I feel like just having an argument about it past this point is needless. If neither of us are going to be able to convince the other, wouldn't it just be better to not waste the time and energy of each other and agree do disagree? I don't believe I am right, or that you are, just that we have different ways in which we would like to handle Avatars in our games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is an entirely appropriate way to handle things, I would really love to see what you come up with. I really do adore looking at other people's house rules, so if you ever devote yours to somewhere online, please let me know. I would love to see your Enech, and your Avatar stuff, but only if it's no bother to you and so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, then we will have to agree to disagree on disagreement. :-) I fully believe we can and should keep on politely grappling with each other rhetorically and maybe one or the other of us will find some argument that will convince the other or continued disagreement will begin to create some alloyed compromises that neither one of us is entirely happy with but that both of us can accept as providing something that our respective viewpoints did not. But then, I'm a lawyer and that's the way rhetoric is SUPPOSED to work. <br /> <br /> In that spirit, here is another line of argumentation. If Scion:God had not included Avatar as a Background, would we be even having this conversation? Unpacking that - would be discussing trying to deal with Legendary Aura, etc. by the idea of the Gods &quot;dumbing themselves down&quot; in this way? I really don't think so. Avatar sensu stricto would have gone into the Devas god-level PSP. Splitting up into little sub-gods into the Mayan. Etc. We would be looking for SOME way to handle the need for gods to travel to Earth incognito to one degree or another, but not THIS way. And we wouldn't be arguing Ares &amp; Aphrodite vs. Diomedes in the Iliad. We would be taking the myths as read and assuming that those rascally two philanderers were there very selves and not some pale, not-enough-toner, copy. <br /> <br /> So, if that is true, then why not dispense with a clunky mechanic that seems to cause as much problem as it solves? And one that really most sincerely does not belong in the vast majority of mythologies it's being inflicted on? <br /> <br /> I'll probably never post things online or on the forum. I keep amending and changing and tweaking and working on any and everything rule-related because they are under continual play-test. I realize I don't have the wherewithal to get a genuine test done. So my ideas are like string-theory. They objectively make sense to me and might handle the problem I've discerned, but there is no way to know whether they will survive contact with actual gaming. And usually they will require some fine-tuning, at best, after they do. Also, after making rules changes on game after game after game (from D&amp;D 2nd ed. on), I've learned that &quot;less is more&quot; is definitely the way to go. I may jot down my ideas for the whole kit and kabodle, but I only make up what I need to to run the game I'm in right now and expand on it as needed. So a new PSP will be the first three boons. A new pantheon will be 10-12 gods. Etc. I don't make up the Titan, the Over &amp; Underworlds, etc. until I need them. Unless it's something that I'm really really into at the moment. <br /> <br /> So, Avatar, no. Current Scion game is about to hit Demigod, so that's WAAAAAY off and it's not something I really care for in any case. <br /> <br /> Enech? Well.... that's a different story. I don't like it on it's face per Irish mythology. I love Irish mythology, so I am somewhat motivated to replace it with something else. I am also playing a Tuatha De Scion right now, so I am having to confront it squarely as we were NOT using it as written. So I worked with Telgar to come up with some alternative. Which is currently being playtested and going... okay. Compared to the rest of the group, the replacement is not super-snazzy or as useful as revised Jontunblut or Arete or Cheval. Enech had more visceral punch but it's more like a badly made sledgehammer than a well-thrown haymaker. <br /> <br /> A Hittite pantheon? That's hard NOT to do, but gathering a decent set of sources is the major issue before I go in whole hog and try to do it. (Probably not the way that Anne was going with it, but I love what she did before she left us &lt;sniff&gt; and went off to do her own thing.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T09:50:57-07:00","id":149452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=149444#post149444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, then we will have to agree to disagree on disagreement. :-) I fully believe we can and should keep on politely grappling with each other rhetorically and maybe one or the other of us will find some argument that will convince the other or continued disagreement will begin to create some alloyed compromises that neither one of us is entirely happy with but that both of us can accept as providing something that our respective viewpoints did not. But then, I'm a lawyer and that's the way rhetoric is SUPPOSED to work. <br /> <br /> In that spirit, here is another line of argumentation. If Scion:God had not included Avatar as a Background, would we be even having this conversation? Unpacking that - would be discussing trying to deal with Legendary Aura, etc. by the idea of the Gods &quot;dumbing themselves down&quot; in this way? I really don't think so. Avatar sensu stricto would have gone into the Devas god-level PSP. Splitting up into little sub-gods into the Mayan. Etc. We would be looking for SOME way to handle the need for gods to travel to Earth incognito to one degree or another, but not THIS way. And we wouldn't be arguing Ares &amp; Aphrodite vs. Diomedes in the Iliad. We would be taking the myths as read and assuming that those rascally two philanderers were there very selves and not some pale, not-enough-toner, copy.<br /> <br /> So, if that is true, then why not dispense with a clunky mechanic that seems to cause as much problem as it solves? And one that really most sincerely does not belong in the vast majority of mythologies it's being inflicted on?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have to chime in and say that your reply Ajax had me and Iry discussing mechanics very early yesterday morning and we actually revised Avatar, again, due to some of the things you pointed out. While we still maintained the ability, it is now far more mythical (at least I think so, but I'm weird and still a little hung-over). So I think polite disagreement works if it promotes discussion and consideration of mechanics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=149444#post149444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enech? Well.... that's a different story. I don't like it on it's face per Irish mythology. I love Irish mythology, so I am somewhat motivated to replace it with something else. I am also playing a Tuatha De Scion right now, so I am having to confront it squarely as we were NOT using it as written. So I worked with Telgar to come up with some alternative. Which is currently being playtested and going... okay. Compared to the rest of the group, the replacement is not super-snazzy or as useful as revised Jontunblut or Arete or Cheval. Enech had more visceral punch but it's more like a badly made sledgehammer than a well-thrown haymaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were sitting around and hoping that JSR would revise Enech and the last game that was run in our group we had two Tuatha but neither one of us picked up RAW Enech because it was terrible; then after JSR's annoucement we went &quot;well, damn it, might as well&quot; and spent a weekend looking up myths, folklore and ... man, I will give props to anyone that does a PSP outside a pantheon they're obsessed with because it's crazy. Crazy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=149444#post149444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hittite pantheon? That's hard NOT to do, but gathering a decent set of sources is the major issue before I go in whole hog and try to do it. (Probably not the way that Anne was going with it, but I love what she did before she left us &lt;sniff&gt; and went off to do her own thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if we can pester her to see which titan they were aiming towards. Actually, I wonder if we can see the &quot;new&quot; four titans they would have had up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:10:16-07:00","id":149470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=149452#post149452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if we can pester her to see which titan they were aiming towards. Actually, I wonder if we can see the &quot;new&quot; four titans they would have had up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally Off-Topic, but I was going with Upellari with a Primary Avatar (och! there's that word again!) of Ullikummi as he seems ideal for the role. He threatened the WHOLE pantheon instead of just a pissing match with Tarhunt (that would be Ilyanka, who probably should be an Avatar of some other Titan....) (Aside: Don't get me started on the Titanomachy as the guiding principle of the whole game, either. You want to wander into an area where I have REALLY strong feelings...)<br /> <br /> Upellari would be the Titanrealm/Greater Titan/Primal Entity of Stone, which would include the idea of stasis to some degree. Opposed to the Purview of Earth (which is more rocks/stone/mountains/wealth as in valuable swag you dig up + dirt, etc.) This is obdurate unyielding stone. Deep below the places where there is ever anything that would support a growing plant and there is ever a breath of air or a gleam of sunlight. Just plain unchanging ROCK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:20:02-07:00","id":149494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/146704-acquiring-the-avatar-birthright-after-god-level-up?p=149470#post149470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally Off-Topic, but I was going with Upellari with a Primary Avatar (och! there's that word again!) of Ullikummi as he seems ideal for the role. He threatened the WHOLE pantheon instead of just a pissing match with Tarhunt (that would be Ilyanka, who probably should be an Avatar of some other Titan....) (Aside: Don't get me started on the Titanomachy as the guiding principle of the whole game, either. You want to wander into an area where I have REALLY strong feelings...)<br /> <br /> Upellari would be the Titanrealm/Greater Titan/Primal Entity of Stone, which would include the idea of stasis to some degree. Opposed to the Purview of Earth (which is more rocks/stone/mountains/wealth as in valuable swag you dig up + dirt, etc.) This is obdurate unyielding stone. Deep below the places where there is ever anything that would support a growing plant and there is ever a breath of air or a gleam of sunlight. Just plain unchanging ROCK.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Scion RAW used Avatar for far too much; I think I took Telgar's route and started calling Titan &quot;Avatars&quot; Aspects just so I wouldn't be so damned confused. And I agree on the Titannomachy; I think I've used it once as a whole? Otherwise games are built from just normal mythology. Oh, Apep ate the sun; oh, Balor's risen and is seeking revenge; oh, Raganrok, ect.<br /> <br /> As all I know of the Hittites is what Anne threw up; my contributions would be looking for antagonists that could be placed within the Greater Titan and how the mechanics could work; but I agree that Upellari isn't really capable of merging with Earth (though I waffled back and forth for a while) because I don't think any other mythology had the earth as such unchanging and yielding; or barren of life. If life didn't come from the waters in mythos, you could almost guarantee it would be from dust/clay/the earth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:40:07-07:00","id":149503,"title":"","content":"Yes, I gathered a few people together and we sat and talked for hours about some of your points about Avatar, Ajax. We went through and tried to hammer down every single way in which mythology had a situation that could be represented with Avatars, how many problems it solved or created to change Avatar, and whether or not Avatar could be completely removed without widespread revision.<br /> <br /> The single biggest obstacle was <b>Fateful Aura</b>, which is why I am interested to hear your thoughts on the matter, Ajax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T13:31:42-07:00","id":149699,"title":"","content":"Before I address it, I'm going to have to winkle out some time to take a long hard look at the rules again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T06:21:49-07:00","id":151239,"title":"","content":"This became so much more than I expected. Thank for everyone who offered their opinion.<br /> <br /> I approached my players Saturday and they all agree that it should simply come with being a god. So, in that way, problem solved.<br /> <br /> I agree though, that it is ultimately an issue of fate bonds and fateful aura when talking about the ramification of Avatar use. The way I see Fateful Aura being balanced is this \u2013 if you're a big enough deal to the cosmos or even just the overworld (implying a high Legend) then your Fateful Aura has created a sort of divine expectation of you from other entities. Thing happen and you've always dealt with them before.<br /> <br /> Your Fateful Aura is like a divine gravity in the vacuum of existence. Once a fated occurrence is triggered and first pulled toward you \u2013 it doesn't stop coming at you. So whether you're Legend 12 and sitting in the overworld or you're Legend 3 and cavorting with mortals down in their realm, that event is still going to happen. If you're refusing to deal with it then someone else likely will, and the resulting fatebonds to them will not go over lightly when they find out what's going on. This is why Justice Gods get super-serious with other gods shirking their &quot;responsibilities.&quot; It's why Order, Duty, Loyalty and to a certain extent Harmony and Piety are the course-correcting Virtues that they are. Sure a God could hypothetically try to stay in Avatar form, but something is going to prompt them back into their true form eventually.<br /> <br /> All Avatar should be expected to do IMO is mitigate fatebonds. Gods are people too, and they're prone to have fun with their abilities when not embroiled in the most serious of Fateful Aura events. Avatar is usually how Gods get to do that and not make the players suffer as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2692-captain-morganism","name":"Captain Morganism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2692_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}